  "final_text": "I can't give you a number yet. There's one open question first.\n\n`customer_master.csv` has 144 accounts, and its `status` column contains three codes: **A**, **C** and **N**. Nothing I have explains what the codes mean, and I couldn't find a metric definitions file for \"active accounts\". If I guessed at the codes, I could get the wrong number.\n\n**Which status codes count as an active account on 30 June 2026?** For example, A only, or A and N? It would also help to know what C and N stand for (perhaps \"churned\" and \"new\").\n\nOne more thing, for when we calculate: this file appears to show each account's current status and the date it last changed (`status_dt`). It doesn't keep a history. No status dates fall after 30 June, so the file should match the 30 June position. That's only true if the export was taken on or close to 1 July.",
